---
title: About LevelUp Civics
description: >-
  Level Up Civics Foundation is a California nonprofit connecting students to real community challenges through game-based civic design.
---
{% extends "layouts/base.njk" %}

{% block head %}
<style>
  /* ── HERO (cream split layout) ─────────────────────────────── */
  .hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 55% 45%;
    padding: 80px 0 0 max(0px, calc(50% - 720px));
  }
  .hero-content {
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center;
    padding: 60px 72px 60px 80px;
    background: var(--cream);
  }
  .hero-visual { overflow: hidden; position: relative; }
  .hero-visual img {
    width: 100%; height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover; object-position: center top;
    display: block;
  }
  .hero-h1 {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(42px, 4.9vw, 66px);
    line-height: 1.02; color: var(--ink); letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .hero-eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 13px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--red); margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .hero-sub {
    font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--gray);
    max-width: 460px; margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .hero-cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .hero-cta-row > a { white-space: nowrap; }

  /* ── INFO CARDS ON NAVY ───────────────────────────────────────── */
  .sec-navy .info-card { border-color: var(--mnav); }
  .sec-navy .info-card-text { color: var(--civic); }

  /* ── TWO-COL MISSION GRID ────────────────────────────────────── */
  .about-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 80px; align-items: start; margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .about-cards-col { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }

  .about-org-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .about-org-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* ── QUOTE BAND (local — mirrors program page) ───────────────── */
  .quote-band { border-top: 4px solid var(--red); background: var(--cream); padding: 80px; }
  .quote-inner { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28% 1fr; gap: 56px; align-items: center; }
  .quote-mark-wrap { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: flex-end; }
  .quote-mark-wrap img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; opacity: 0.12; }
  .quote-text {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.8vw, 40px);
    color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .quote-attr { font-size: 14px; color: var(--gray); line-height: 1.6; }
  .quote-attr strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

  /* ── PARTNER LOGO PLACEHOLDER ────────────────────────────────── */
  .partner-logo-wrap {
    height: 56px; background: var(--soft);
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .partner-logo-wrap span {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gray);
  }

  /* ── TEAM GRID ───────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .team-grid {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 32px; margin-top: 48px;
  }
  .team-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .team-photo {
    width: 100%; aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
    object-fit: cover; object-position: top center;
    display: block; margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .team-name {
    font-family: 'Big Shoulders Display', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700; font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .team-role {
    font-family: 'Pixelify Sans', sans-serif; font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gray);
  }

  /* ── RESPONSIVE ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr; height: auto; min-height: unset; }
    .hero-content { padding: 52px 48px 56px; }
    .hero-visual { height: 400px; }
    .hero-visual img { object-position: center center; }
    .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 48px; }
    .team-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 24px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .hero-content { padding: 44px 20px 48px; }
    .hero-visual { height: 280px; }
    .hero-cta-row { flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .quote-band { padding: 64px 20px; }
    .quote-inner { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
    .quote-mark-wrap img { max-width: 72px; opacity: 0.08; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .hero-visual { height: 240px; }
    .hero-cta-row { flex-direction: column; }
    .team-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}

<!-- HERO -->
<div class="hero">
  <div class="hero-content">
    <div class="hero-eyebrow">About</div>
    <h1 class="hero-h1">Student ideas should reach the people in charge.</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Level Up Civics Foundation is a California nonprofit. We connect students to real community challenges through game-based civic design, and we bring together the educators, county offices of education, local government and technology partners it takes to get a student&#39;s idea in front of someone who can act on it.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-cta-row">
      <a href="/program/" class="btn-primary">See the Program</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-visual">
    <img src="/assets/hero-image.png" alt="Level Up Civics students competing">
  </div>
</div>

<!-- WHAT WE BELIEVE -->
<section class="sec sec-navy">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-light page-h2 h2-body">What we believe.</h2>
  <div class="about-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="sec-body">Level Up Civics gives students a real community problem, a game-based world to build their solution in, and a real decision-maker to pitch it to. When students know their ideas can reach the people in charge, an assignment becomes advocacy.</p>
      <p class="sec-body">The principle behind the program: a specific place, a specific problem, and an audience who will actually turn up produce better student work than an open prompt. What comes out the other side are students who have investigated something, designed for it, built it, and argued for it in public.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="about-cards-col">
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">The problem</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">A real community challenge in their own county rather than a fictional scenario</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">The world</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">A Minecraft Education environment built around their actual county</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">The audience</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">Local leaders who are in the room to listen as much as to judge</p>
      </div>
      <div class="info-card">
        <div class="info-card-lbl">The result</div>
        <p class="info-card-text">Civic confidence and work habits that outlast the class they were learned in</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- THE ORGANIZATION AND THE PROGRAM -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <div class="sec-header">
    <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2">The nonprofit and the program</h2>
    <p class="sec-header-intro">These two names get used interchangeably, so it is worth separating them. One is the organization. The other is what it currently runs.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="about-org-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-dark">The organization</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Level Up Civics Foundation</h3>
      <p class="card-body">A California nonprofit, 501(c)(3) status pending. Our work is getting students into real civic problems and getting their proposals in front of the people who decide. Battle of the Counties is how we do that today. It is not the whole of what the foundation is for.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-eyebrow card-eyebrow-red">The flagship program</div>
      <h3 class="card-title">Schools Reinventing Counties &amp; Battle of the Counties</h3>
      <p class="card-body">Our current flagship experience. Schools Reinventing Counties is the Minecraft Education world and the learning inside it. Battle of the Counties is the academic esports competition built around it, running through the Statewide Championship on January 9, 2027.</p>
      <a href="/program/" class="card-link-text" style="display:inline-block; text-decoration:none;">See how the two fit together &#8594;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- QUOTE -->
<div class="quote-band">
  <div class="quote-inner">
    <div class="quote-mark-wrap">
      <img src="/assets/quote-mark.svg" alt="">
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="quote-text">"This is not about playing a game. It is about student voice, civic engagement, and showing our students that their ideas can lead real change."</p>
      <div class="quote-attr"><strong>Dr. Stefan Bean</strong>, Orange County Superintendent of Schools</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- WHO WE BRING TOGETHER -->
<section class="sec sec-navy">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-light page-h2 h2-block">Who we bring together.</h2>
  <div class="grid-3">
    <div class="pillar">
      <div class="pillar-num">01</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">County Offices of Education</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">County education offices anchor the program. When a county commits, the world gets built and every school in that region gets access. The county brings the institutional credibility, the licensing coordination, and somewhere to hold the event.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar">
      <div class="pillar-num">02</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Sponsors and Grant Funders</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Mission-aligned organizations fund the county world builds and program operations. Each world is a one-time build that then serves cohort after cohort. It behaves more like infrastructure than like a program you have to fund again every year.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar">
      <div class="pillar-num">03</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">City and County Government</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Local government partners bring a genuine community challenge and a commitment to show up and hear what students propose. Their presence is what raises the stakes. Students pitch to people who can act on what they hear.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar">
      <div class="pillar-num">04</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Educators</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Teachers facilitate the design process. The worlds come built and the rounds come structured, so educators can take students through investigation, design and advocacy without building anything themselves.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar">
      <div class="pillar-num">05</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Build Partners</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Lifeboat Studios builds every county world on real local geography, landmarks, and community life using Minecraft Education, with no work required from school staff.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillar">
      <div class="pillar-num">06</div>
      <h3 class="pillar-title">Students</h3>
      <p class="pillar-body">Grades 3–12 students across California who investigate real challenges, build solutions, and pitch their ideas to the leaders making decisions in their communities. The whole program is built around what happens when they know their work matters.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- TEAM -->
<section class="sec sec-cream">
  <h2 class="sec-h2 sec-h2-dark page-h2">The team.</h2>
  <div class="team-grid">
    <div class="team-card">
      <img src="/assets/jason-collar.jpg" alt="Jason Collar" class="team-photo">
      <div class="team-name">Jason Collar</div>
      <div class="team-role">CEO</div>
    </div>
    <div class="team-card">
      <img src="/assets/chris-lowe.jpg" alt="Chris Lowe" class="team-photo">
      <div class="team-name">Chris Lowe</div>
      <div class="team-role">COO</div>
    </div>
    <div class="team-card">
      <img src="/assets/michael-matsuda.jpg" alt="Michael Matsuda" class="team-photo">
      <div class="team-name">Michael Matsuda</div>
      <div class="team-role">Education Advisor</div>
    </div>
    <div class="team-card">
      <img src="/assets/peter-polygalov.jpg" alt="Peter Polygalov" class="team-photo">
      <div class="team-name">Peter Polygalov</div>
      <div class="team-role">Marketing & Comms Lead</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- CTA BAND -->
<div class="cta-band">
  <div class="cta-band-inner">
    <h2 class="cta-band-h2">Get in touch.</h2>
    <p class="cta-band-body">
      For partnership inquiries, program questions, or press, reach us at info@levelupcivicsfoundation.org. Level Up Civics Foundation is a California nonprofit. 501(c)(3) status pending.
    </p>
    <div class="cta-band-btns">
      <a href="/partners/" class="btn-white">Partner with us →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

{% endblock %}
